          "id": 1488384323,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "In this case, 'the_bits' are only 10 bits, and these fields are picking out subsets of these 10 bits.\n\nI am wondering if I should even warn about the field width vs length when proto_tree_add_uint() is used - what do you think?\n\n- sometimes the value needs less as it only really uses a subset of the highlighted bits (this case).\n- in another case, it might even multiply what is in the selected bytes so the field width needs to be even wider.",
